oute has atmospheric/chemical critiques, but demonstrates entirety of proline skeleton from C1/C2/C3 precursors.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"rxn_002\",\n      \"name\": \"Thermal condensation of formaldehyde and ammonia (Fox\u2013Windsor route)\",\n      \"inputs\": [\"mol_005\", \"mol_004\"],\n      \"outputs\": [\"mol_019\"],\n      \"environment\": \"Surface\",\n      \"agents\": [null],\n      \"conditions\": {\n        \"temperature\": \"450K (185\u00b0C)\",\n        \"pressure\": \"ambient\",\n        \"catalyst\": null,\n        \"aqueous\": true,\n        \"other\": \"Acid hydrolysis required post-reaction\"\n      },\n      \"mechanism\": \"Repeated C\u2013C condensation and nitrogen incorporation form polymeric/hydrolysable intermediates, hydrolysis liberates proline along with other amino acids.\",\n      \"reasoning\": \"Fox & Windsor (1970) and Wolman et al. (1971): amino acid mixture (incl. proline) released after hydrolysis, no mineral catalyst; mechanistically unresolved for the proline ring, but experimentally detected endpoint. Hydrolysis blank controls required; product is not free proline in environment.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"rxn_003\",\n      \"name\": \"Formaldehyde\u2013hydroxylamine condensation with transition metals, MoO4^2\u2212, and clays (Hatanaka\u2013Egami route)\",\n      \"inputs\": [\"mol_005\", \"mol_008\", \"mol_018\"],\n      \"outputs\": [\"mol_019\"],\n      \"environment\": \"Surface\",\n      \"agents\": [\"Montmorillonite\", \"Kaolin\", \"MoO4^2\u2212\", \"Zn2+\", \"Fe3+\", \"Cu2+\", \"Co2+\", \"Mn2+\"],\n      \"conditions\": {\n        \"temperature\": \"378K (105\u00b0C)\",\n        \"pressure\": \"ambient\",\n        \"catalyst\": \"MoO4^2\u2212, clays, metals\",\n        \"aqueous\": true,\n        \"other\": \"Acid hydrolysis; pH 5.5; 7 d reaction\"\n      },\n      \"mechanism\": \"Formaldehyde and hydroxylamine react to give N-rich oligomers, transition metals and molybdate shift selectivity towards