ueous\": false,\n        \"other\": \"High-energy proton irradiation\"\n      },\n      \"mechanism\": \"Radical-induced polymerization and rearrangement under irradiation followed by hydrolysis liberates amino acids, including proline, from formamide and meteorite mixture.\",\n      \"reasoning\": \"Saladino et al. (2015): Proline detected uniquely in the irradiation/meteorite/formamide regime. Radical mechanism and product assignments require further isotope study for full mechanistic resolution.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"rxn_011\",\n      \"name\": \"UV-irradiated interstellar/pre-cometary ice (Mu\u00f1oz Caro, Bernstein routes)\",\n      \"inputs\": [\"mol_003\", \"mol_004\", \"mol_001\", \"mol_013\"],\n      \"outputs\": [\"mol_019\"],\n      \"environment\": \"Surface\",\n      \"agents\": [\"UV irradiation\", null],\n      \"conditions\": {\n        \"temperature\": \"12K (formation); warming to 300K\",\n        \"pressure\": \"high vacuum then ambient\",\n        \"catalyst\": null,\n        \"aqueous\": false,\n        \"other\": \"Hydrolysis after warm-up\"\n      },\n      \"mechanism\": \"UV creates radical-rich environment in ice, forming complex organic residue; warm-up and hydrolysis releases proline among amino acids.\",\n      \"reasoning\": \"Mu\u00f1oz Caro et al. (2002); Bernstein et al. (2002): Isotope-labeled detection; proline among release products. Mechanistic intermediates for proline ring in solid-state are unassigned. Racemic product distribution.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"rxn_012\",\n      \"name\": \"Chiral enrichment (speculative)\",\n      \"inputs\": [\"mol_019\"],\n      \"outputs\": [\"mol_015\"],\n      \"environment\": \"Biochemical\",\n      \"agents\": [null],\n      \"conditions\": {\n        \"temperature\": \"variable\",\n        \"pressure\": \"variable\",\n        \"catalyst\": null,\n        \"aqueous\": true,\n        \"other\": \"Possible physical/chemical symmetry breaking\"\n      },\n      \"mechanism