gh formamide activity required.\",\n      \"approved\": false,\n      \"problematic_reactions\": [\"rxn_012\"],\n      \"suggestions\": [\n        \"Clarify the intermediate sequence (aminonitrile/radical steps)\",\n        \"Balance the reaction explicitly\",\n        \"Justify the prebiotic plausibility of neat formamide or offer alternatives\"\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"pathway_id\": \"P6\",\n      \"reaction_scores\": {\n        \"rxn_013\": 0.5\n      },\n      \"chemical_feasibility\": 0.5,\n      \"pathway_coherence\": 0.7,\n      \"environmental_progression\": 0.9,\n      \"target_achievement\": 0.65,\n      \"overall_confidence\": 0.65,\n      \"feedback\": \"Astrochemical UV ice chemistry reproduces prebiotic astrochemical findings (Mu\u00f1oz Caro et al.). The reaction (rxn_013) is unbalanced. The literature supports production of proline after hydrolysis, and this is depicted as a two-step module. Environmental consistency is strong (surface/ice irradiation). Mechanistically, the step from C1 precursors to proline is abstracted, so pathway detail is weak.\",\n      \"approved\": false,\n      \"problematic_reactions\": [\"rxn_013\"],\n      \"suggestions\": [\n        \"Balance the overall stoichiometry\",\n        \"Clarify which intermediates (aminonitrile, macromolecule, amino acid) are present before hydrolysis\",\n        \"Indicate the expected racemic outcome\"\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"pathway_id\": \"P7\",\n      \"reaction_scores\": {\n        \"rxn_004\": 0.6,\n        \"rxn_005\": 0.75,\n        \"rxn_006\": 0.5,\n        \"rxn_007\": 0.45,\n        \"rxn_008\": 0.4,\n        \"rxn_009\": 0.45,\n        \"rxn_010\": 0.4,\n        \"rxn_014\": 0.65\n      },\n      \"chemical_feasibility\": 0.5,\n      \"pathway_coherence\": 0.85,\n      \"environmental_progression\": 0.85,\n      \"target_achievement\": 0.8,\n      \"overall_confidence\": 0.8,\n      \"feedback\": \"This multi-step sequence (Patel-style) models the clearest known